IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgh-returns`

-- Tests for sgh-returns.l4 (ss 13 to 15). Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion, before the run.

§ `s 13: enforcement of the duty to make returns`
-- (test alias a13f = `s 13(1) the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice`)
-- arguments: the day the notice was served; the day the default was made good, if it was
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS TRUE   -- never made good
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) EQUALS FALSE   -- made good on the 14th day after service (1 March plus 14 days is 15 March): within 14 days after
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 16 3 2026)) EQUALS TRUE   -- made good one day later: not within 14 days after
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the corporation or person failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 3 2026)) EQUALS FALSE   -- made good on the day of service: in time (fork line F-H-P2)
-- (test alias a13a = `s 13(1) the Court may order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default`)
-- arguments: default under (a); the requirement is imposed by the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018; default under (b); default under (c); failed to make good within 14 days; applicant is a member, a creditor or the Registrar
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the Court may order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) any provision of this Act or of any other law ... which requires the filing or lodging ... of any return, account or other document", failing to make good within 14 days, on application by a member or creditor or by the Registrar
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the Court may order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) any request of the Registrar to amend or complete and resubmit any document or to submit a fresh document"
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the Court may order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(c) any request of the Registrar under section 12D(7)"
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the Court may order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "(other than the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018)": paragraph (a) is closed in the text's own words
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the Court may order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- under the IRDA for (a), but a default under (b) stands alone
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the Court may order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- made good in time: a failed "If" gating a grant (grant ruling, limit 1)
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the Court may order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the applicant is none of the three: limited by its own wording
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the Court may order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a default of no kind the subsection names: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a13b = `s 13(2) the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the bearer`)
-- arguments: an order under subsection (1); the bearer; the officer is responsible for the default
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the bearer` TRUE `s 13(2) the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "must be borne by the corporation"
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the bearer` TRUE `s 13(2) such person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or by such person"
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the bearer` TRUE `s 13(2) an officer of the corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "by any officer of the corporation responsible for the default"
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the bearer` TRUE `s 13(2) an officer of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an officer not responsible: limited by its own wording
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the bearer` TRUE `s 13(2) someone else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another bearer: the list does not say "only" (list not closed)
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the bearer` FALSE `s 13(2) the corporation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an order under subsection (1): "Any such order"
-- (test alias a13c = `s 13(3) this section limits the operation of the written law`)
#ASSERT `s 13(3) this section limits the operation of the written law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Nothing in this section limits the operation of any written law imposing penalties"
#ASSERT `s 13(3) this section limits the operation of the written law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another law: the text says nothing

§ `s 14: relodging of lost registered documents`
-- (test alias a14a = `s 14(1) the corporation may apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged`)
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the corporation may apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the constitution or any other document relating to the corporation filed or lodged with the Registrar has been lost or destroyed"
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the corporation may apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- nothing lost or destroyed: a failed "If" gating a grant (grant ruling, limit 1)
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the corporation may apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not incorporated or registered under this Act or a corresponding previous law: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a14b = `s 14(2) the Registrar may direct notice of the application to be given to such persons and in such manner as the Registrar thinks fit`)
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the Registrar may direct notice of the application to be given to such persons and in such manner as the Registrar thinks fit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "On such application being made the Registrar may direct notice thereof to be given"
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the Registrar may direct notice of the application to be given to such persons and in such manner as the Registrar thinks fit` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application made: a failed "when" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
-- (test alias a14c = `s 14(3) the Registrar may certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original`)
-- arguments: satisfied it is lost or destroyed; satisfied of the date of the filing or lodging; satisfied the copy is correct
#ASSERT `s 14(3) the Registrar may certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." all met
#ASSERT `s 14(3) the Registrar may certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) unmet: a failed "upon being satisfied" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
#ASSERT `s 14(3) the Registrar may certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) unmet
#ASSERT `s 14(3) the Registrar may certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c) unmet
-- (test alias a14d = `s 14(4) the copy has for all purposes the same force and effect as the original`)
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the copy has for all purposes the same force and effect as the original` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Upon the lodgment, that copy for all purposes has ... the same force and effect as the original"
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the copy has for all purposes the same force and effect as the original` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not lodged: a failed "upon" (periods ruling (b))
-- (test alias a14e = `s 14(4) the date from which the copy has the same force and effect as the original`)
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the date from which the copy has the same force and effect as the original` TRUE (Date 1 6 2020) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 6 2020)   -- "from such date as is mentioned in the certificate as the date of the filing or lodging of the original"
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the date from which the copy has the same force and effect as the original` FALSE (Date 1 6 2020) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not lodged: the text names no date
-- (test alias a14f = `s 14(5) the Court may by order confirm, vary or rescind the certificate`)
-- arguments: a person aggrieved has applied; notice given to any other person the Court directs
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the Court may by order confirm, vary or rescind the certificate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "upon application by any person aggrieved and after notice to any other person whom the Court directs"
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the Court may by order confirm, vary or rescind the certificate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application: a failed "upon" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the Court may by order confirm, vary or rescind the certificate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no notice: a failed "after" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
-- (test alias a14g = `s 14(5) the order of the Court may be lodged with the Registrar`)
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the order of the Court may be lodged with the Registrar` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the order may be lodged with the Registrar"
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the order of the Court may be lodged with the Registrar` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an order under this subsection: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a14h = `s 14(5) the Registrar must register the order`)
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the Registrar must register the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "must be registered by the Registrar"
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the Registrar must register the order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not lodged: the duty does not arise (marginal reading (a))
-- (test alias a14i = `s 14(5) the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing is invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission`)
-- arguments: the order varies or rescinds the certificate; in good faith; before the registration of the order; upon the faith of and in reliance upon the certificate
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing is invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "no payments, contracts, dealings, acts and things made, had or done in good faith before the registration of such order and upon the faith of and in reliance upon the certificate are invalidated or affected"
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing is invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in good faith: the saving does not speak
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing is invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- after the registration of the order: the saving does not speak
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing is invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in reliance upon the certificate: the saving does not speak
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing is invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no variation or rescission: the sentence does not speak
-- (test alias a14j = `s 14(6) a fee is payable upon the lodging of the document`)
#ASSERT `s 14(6) a fee is payable upon the lodging of the document` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "No fee is payable upon the lodging of a document under this section"
#ASSERT `s 14(6) a fee is payable upon the lodging of the document` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a document lodged otherwise: the text says nothing

§ `s 15: size, durability and legibility of documents`
-- (test alias a15a = `s 15(2) the Registrar may serve on the person a notice stating the Registrar's opinion and the requirements with which the document does not comply`)
-- arguments: a document delivered under a provision of the Act; in the Registrar's opinion it does not comply; the person is one by whom the document was required to be delivered
#ASSERT `s 15(2) the Registrar may serve on the person a notice stating the Registrar's opinion and the requirements with which the document does not comply` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the Registrar may serve on any person by whom under that provision the document was required to be delivered ... a notice"
#ASSERT `s 15(2) the Registrar may serve on the person a notice stating the Registrar's opinion and the requirements with which the document does not comply` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a person who was not required to deliver it: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 15(2) the Registrar may serve on the person a notice stating the Registrar's opinion and the requirements with which the document does not comply` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the Registrar holds no such opinion: a failed "If" gating a grant (grant ruling, limit 1)
#ASSERT `s 15(2) the Registrar may serve on the person a notice stating the Registrar's opinion and the requirements with which the document does not comply` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no document delivered under the Act: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a15b = `s 15(3)(a) the duty to deliver the document is treated as not having been discharged by the delivery of that document`)
#ASSERT `s 15(3)(a) the duty to deliver the document is treated as not having been discharged by the delivery of that document` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "any duty imposed by that provision to deliver such a document to the Registrar is to be treated as not having been discharged by the delivery of that document"
#ASSERT `s 15(3)(a) the duty to deliver the document is treated as not having been discharged by the delivery of that document` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no notice served under subsection (2): a failed "Where" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii)); the answer means only that this deeming does not apply
-- (test alias a15c = `s 15(4) the last day of the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)`)
-- arguments: the day on which the document was delivered; the date of service of the notice
#ASSERT `s 15(4) the last day of the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) EQUALS Date 24 2 2026   -- "ending on the 14th day after the date of service of the notice": 10 February plus 14 days is 24 February
#ASSERT `s 15(4) the last day of the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 20 2 2026) EQUALS Date 6 3 2026   -- 20 February plus 14 days is 6 March (28 days in February 2026)
-- (test alias a15d = `s 15(4) the day falls within the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)`)
-- arguments: the day the document was delivered; the date of service of the notice; the day
#ASSERT `s 15(4) the day falls within the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) EQUALS TRUE   -- "beginning on the day on which the document was delivered": the first day is in the period
#ASSERT `s 15(4) the day falls within the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 24 2 2026) EQUALS TRUE   -- the 14th day after service is the last day in the period
#ASSERT `s 15(4) the day falls within the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 25 2 2026) EQUALS FALSE   -- the day after the 14th day: outside
#ASSERT `s 15(4) the day falls within the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS FALSE   -- the day before the document was delivered: outside
-- (test alias a15e = `s 15(3)(b) no account is taken of the day in applying a penalty imposed by reference to each day during which the omission continues`)
-- arguments: a notice served under (2); the day the document was delivered; the date of service; the day
#ASSERT `s 15(3)(b) no account is taken of the day in applying a penalty imposed by reference to each day during which the omission continues` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 15 2 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "no account is to be taken of any days falling within the period mentioned in subsection (4)"
#ASSERT `s 15(3)(b) no account is taken of the day in applying a penalty imposed by reference to each day during which the omission continues` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 25 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after the period ends: a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `s 15(3)(b) no account is taken of the day in applying a penalty imposed by reference to each day during which the omission continues` FALSE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 15 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no notice served: a failed "Where" (periods ruling (b))
-- (test alias a15f = `s 15(5) the act is a delivery of the document`)
-- arguments: the act; the document is a notice
#ASSERT `s 15(5) the act is a delivery of the document` `s 15(5) delivering the document` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "any reference to delivering a document"
#ASSERT `s 15(5) the act is a delivery of the document` `s 15(5) sending the document` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "including a reference to sending"
#ASSERT `s 15(5) the act is a delivery of the document` `s 15(5) forwarding the document` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "forwarding"
#ASSERT `s 15(5) the act is a delivery of the document` `s 15(5) producing the document` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "producing"
#ASSERT `s 15(5) the act is a delivery of the document` `s 15(5) giving the document` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or (in the case of a notice) giving it"
#ASSERT `s 15(5) the act is a delivery of the document` `s 15(5) giving the document` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- giving a document that is not a notice: "includes" leaves the term open
#ASSERT `s 15(5) the act is a delivery of the document` `s 15(5) some other act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another act: "includes" leaves the term open

§ `Regulative rule of s 14(5): no time and no consequence the text states, so the s 52 input sets the time`
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 14(5) rule: the Registrar's duty to register the order` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 14(5) register the order of the Court lodged with the Registrar` AT 900

-- in time: the act is done on day 5 and the input is 45 days, so there is no breach
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 14(5) rule: the Registrar's duty to register the order` 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 14(5) register the order of the Court lodged with the Registrar` AT 5

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 14(5) rule: the Registrar's duty to register the order` 45 AT 0 WITH
